Z||000000||b lo 0||09-12-2001||01:30 AM||||I need to put a breather filter on the 2.8, as the PCV leaks, and I want the look of a breather.  I can't find anywhere that sells the PCV.  V8 breathers are too big, so I decided to go with a ricer-style female small breather from Pep Boys.  Since the PCV is straight, I figured I'd put the breather on the PCV, delete the hosing, and plug the hole in the intake.  I'll post pics and let yall know how it works.  Opinions?<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">       <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.vstoreauto.com.com" TARGET=_blank>Audio Imagery</A>, budget-priced car audio supplies from people like Monster Cable, Sony & more!||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||09-12-2001||04:29 PM||||Okay, I'll confess my ignorance...  are you talking about putting a breather (I'm thinking a little air filter) on the forward valve cover?  And leaving the PCV valve+ tube in place on the aft valve cover?<P>||||reg||5
Z||000002||NEPTUNE||09-12-2001||04:44 PM||||bad idea- no horsepower gain, will make a mess of your engine compartment with oily fumes, and I think most of us humans like to breathe clean air.||||reg||13
Z||000003||theogre||09-12-2001||06:33 PM||||PCV is as much to protect the engine from those fumes as it is to protect the environment. A "breather" will not force feed fresh air thru the system. That means those fumes will remain in the engine and react with the oil and everything else.<P>As stated above, breathers typically dump oil. W/O the PCV, fumes build pressure in the crank case and it's got to go some place. It nearly always drags oil with it.<P>The aftermarket breathers are made to replace the intake filter that is usually in the air cleaner. They aren't ment for systems w/o PCV...<P>Because it's an emmisions device, ditching a PCV system is illegal.||||reg||1
Z||000004||b lo 0||09-12-2001||06:34 PM||||Umm, you don't seem to understand.  The breather I put on is ON the PCV valve.  The valve is still there, and the filter attaches to the top.  Just keeps oil from going into the intake.  I just plugged the pipe that used to go back to the PCV.  Problem is, now I have a tiny bit of oil smoke coming from the forward valve cover.  Is there something else I need to do?  Another breather on the forward cover?  If anyone else has breather filters, help would be greatly appreciated.  Thanks.||||reg||1
